      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1ac5bb70159f40b4933a4602b77732168c" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>uint32_t</type>
        <definition>uint32_t terminal::CSI::subSeparatorBits</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>subSeparatorBits</name>
        <qualifiedname>terminal::CSI::subSeparatorBits</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>{ 0 }</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Bitmask tracking which parameters were preceded by a colon sub-separator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Bit N is set if the separator before parameter N was &apos;:&apos; rather than &apos;;&apos;. For example, in <computeroutput>38:2:255:0:0</computeroutput>, bits 1, 2, 3, 4 would be set (indices 1-4 had colons before them).</para>
<para>This enables dispatch handlers to distinguish between:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>38;5;1</computeroutput> (indexed color: 38 ; 5 ; palette_index)</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>38:2::255:0:0</computeroutput> (RGB color: 38 : 2 : : R : G : B)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a1efed907e307b75536e3fd94244b0bff" kindref="member">isSubSeparator()</ref> to check a specific parameter position </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
