        <referencedby refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a58906bacf120dd611ab969af1a46c1bd" compoundref="_c_s_i_8h" startline="292" endline="299">reset</referencedby>
      </memberdef>
      <memberdef kind="variable" id="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a91d13ea91357c8ab601596bc9da18063" prot="public" static="no" mutable="no">
        <type>bool</type>
        <definition>bool terminal::CSI::hasAccumulator</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>hasAccumulator</name>
        <qualifiedname>terminal::CSI::hasAccumulator</qualifiedname>
        <initializer>{ false }</initializer>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Flag indicating whether <computeroutput><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1ab4ca2a0bec07ba138196a3e62dd27c10" kindref="member">accumulator</ref></computeroutput> contains valid data. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This is false until the first digit is added. It distinguishes between:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>No parameter specified (hasAccumulator = false) -&gt; use default</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_parameter" kindref="compound">Parameter</ref> is zero (hasAccumulator = true, accumulator = 0)</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>For example, in <computeroutput>ESC[;5m</computeroutput>, the first parameter has no digits, so hasAccumulator is false when the separator is encountered. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
