    <sectiondef kind="public-func">
      <memberdef kind="function" id="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a8a3f0c7648031f973e5bb63fd1f81a06" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="yes" noexcept="yes" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>void</type>
        <definition>void terminal::CSI::addDigit</definition>
        <argsstring>(uint8_t digit) noexcept</argsstring>
        <name>addDigit</name>
        <qualifiedname>terminal::CSI::addDigit</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>uint8_t</type>
          <declname>digit</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Adds a digit to the current parameter accumulator. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Called by the parser for each numeric character &apos;0&apos;-&apos;9&apos; in the <ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i" kindref="compound">CSI</ref> parameter string. The digit is incorporated into <computeroutput><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1ab4ca2a0bec07ba138196a3e62dd27c10" kindref="member">accumulator</ref></computeroutput> using base-10 arithmetic.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Overflow Behavior</title><para>If the accumulated value exceeds 65535 (uint16_t max), it wraps modulo 65536. This matches xterm behavior for excessively large parameters.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>digit</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The numeric value of the digit character (0-9). The parser is responsible for converting &apos;0&apos;-&apos;9&apos; to 0-9.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>READER THREAD only.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="par"><title>Example</title><para><programlisting><codeline><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Parsing<sp/>&quot;123&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a8a3f0c7648031f973e5bb63fd1f81a06" kindref="member">addDigit</ref>(1);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>accumulator<sp/>=<sp/>1</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a8a3f0c7648031f973e5bb63fd1f81a06" kindref="member">addDigit</ref>(2);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>accumulator<sp/>=<sp/>12</highlight><highlight class="normal"></highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"><ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i_1a8a3f0c7648031f973e5bb63fd1f81a06" kindref="member">addDigit</ref>(3);<sp/><sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>accumulator<sp/>=<sp/>123</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
