        <name>reset</name>
        <qualifiedname>terminal::CSI::reset</qualifiedname>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Resets the accumulator to initial state for a new <ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i" kindref="compound">CSI</ref> sequence. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Called after a <ref refid="structterminal_1_1_c_s_i" kindref="compound">CSI</ref> sequence has been fully processed (dispatched) to prepare for the next sequence. All fields are reset to their default values.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="par"><title>Performance</title><para>This method uses <computeroutput>std::array::fill()</computeroutput> which is typically optimized to a memset or vectorized store. The struct is small enough that this is negligible in the parsing path.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>READER THREAD only. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="note"><para>Must be called before reusing the accumulator for a new sequence. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
        </detaileddescription>
